From feb016abee9cb4dcda2b55107e91211a897ade6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AssassinK786 <85348050+AssassinK786@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:03:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 7-series: View Implemented Design for Vivado builds through
 implview, the open 7-series flow (openXC7), Cross-Check against the bitstream

- View Implemented Design (FPGA) of an AMD Vivado build: the fpgaview step runs implview export --detail on build/post_route.dcp (server/implview.js); core/implview-model.js makes implview's design and device files the view's model (family-neutral tiles on Vivado's grid, LUT equations from INIT and pin map, flip-flop settings, nets with their route tiles, clock nets).
- The open 7-series flow (synthesis tool openxc7, server/openxc7.js, core/openxc7.js): Yosys synth_xilinx, nextpnr-xilinx, fasm2frames, xc7frames2bit in build/openxc7; its reports and its FPGA view (implview import-nextpnr with nextpnr's INITs and routes).
- Cross-Check (process, POST /projects/:p/crosscheck, MCP cross_check; server/crosscheck.js, core/crosscheck-fasm.js): implview crosscheck of a Vivado build; an open build's bitstream decoded by bit2fasm against nextpnr's FASM and re-encoded against its frames; both builds compared; UltraScale+ / Versal not cross-checkable.
- MCP fpga_view; set_design_properties synth_tool openxc7; Portuguese labels; tests (implview-model, openxc7, crosscheck-fasm, mcp-implview) with fixtures from blinky's Arty S7-25 build; changelog fragment (its issue number a placeholder, 9000).
